{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_templates",
  "description": "Expression-template library for the CISM-specific pointwise laws of the stage-2 CISM components (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00.002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch). Carries the pieces of the CISM basal traction and flow-factor physics that have no PISM/EqIce counterpart and are therefore not in the EqIce template libraries: (a) the bed-elevation friction-angle ramp of the PSEUDO_PLASTIC_OLD basal law (glissade_basal_traction.F90:256-277): phi = phimin below bedmin, phi = phimax above bedmax, and a linear ramp phi = phimin + (bed - bedmin)/(bedmax - bedmin) * (phimax - phimin) in between (the glide_types defaults are pseudo_plastic_phimin = 5 deg, pseudo_plastic_phimax = 40 deg, pseudo_plastic_bedmin = -300 m, pseudo_plastic_bedmax = 700 m, glide_types.F90:2380-2383), and (b) the pressure-corrected temperature construction of the Paterson-Budd flow law (glissade_therm.F90:2596-2598): tempcor = clamp(temp - pmptemp, -50, 0) degC, where temp is the ice temperature and pmptemp the pressure melting point temperature in the same column (pmptemp = -rhoi*grav*pmlt*thck*stagsigma, glissade_therm.F90:2170). The rest of the CISM basal and rheology physics is the same law as PISM's and is imported by reference from the EqIce libraries (../../eqice/stage2/basal_templates.esm: the Bueler & van Pelt / Tulaczyk effective pressure and the pseudo-plastic drag; ../../eqice/stage2/ice_rheology_templates.esm: the Paterson-Budd softness) with the CISM constants bound at the call sites. All templates here are match-less and invoked by name via apply_expression_template."
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "cism_phi_ramp": {
   "description": "Friction angle phi(bed) of the HO_BABC_PSEUDO_PLASTIC_OLD basal law (glissade_basal_traction.F90:256-277): phi = phimin where bed <= bedmin, phi = phimax where bed >= bedmax, and the linear ramp phi = phimin + (bed - bedmin)/(bedmax - bedmin) * (phimax - phimin) in between. bed is the bed elevation topg - eus [m] (with the CELL-CENTER topg, not stagtopg - the known quirk of this deprecated law, glissade_basal_traction.F90:261-263 and bugs.md #23, reproduced here); phimin/phimax are in degrees and bedmin/bedmax in m. CISM-specific: EqIce derives phi from data or inversion rather than from a bed-elevation ramp (CISM_LANE.md row 8).",
   "params": [
    "bed",
    "phimin",
    "phimax",
    "bedmin",
    "bedmax"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<=",
      "args": [
       "bed",
       "bedmin"
      ]
     },
     "phimin",
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
         "bed",
         "bedmax"
        ]
       },
       "phimax",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "phimin",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "bed",
               "bedmin"
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "bedmax",
               "bedmin"
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "phimax",
             "phimin"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_tempcor": {
   "description": "Pressure-corrected temperature of the FLWA_PATERSON_BUDD flow law (glissade_therm.F90:2596-2598): tempcor = min(0, temp - pmptemp), then tempcor = max(-50, tempcor) - i.e. clamp(temp - pmptemp, -50, 0) degC, with temp the ice temperature and pmptemp the pressure melting point temperature in the same layer (both degC, pmptemp <= 0). CISM-specific construction: PISM's Paterson-Budd law takes the pressure-adjusted absolute temperature directly; CISM clamps T - T_pmp to [-50, 0] degC before adding the 273.15 K offset (CISM_LANE.md row 4: 'small variant in the T* construction').",
   "params": [
    "temp",
    "pmptemp"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "max",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": -50.0,
      "units": "degC"
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "degC"
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "temp",
         "pmptemp"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}
